    <string name="page_network">Network</string>
    <string name="network_switch_title">Network</string>
    <string name="network_on_summary">On: it can go online. Only when you tap “Install” or “Check for updates”, and what you type never leaves this device.</string>
    <string name="network_off_summary">Off (the default): fully offline. Neither the store nor the update check runs.</string>
    <string name="network_on_detail">Every connection that really happens is written into the log on the Network page, so you can check for yourself. One more thing worth knowing: while this is on, the moment a connection really happens, your network can see which domain this device reached — DNS lookups and TLS connection targets travel in the clear and we cannot change that. Our requests do not carry this app\'s name, but “did it connect at all” cannot be hidden.</string>

    <!-- %1$s = 「download keyboards」這類動詞片語，見下面的 network_what_*。 -->
    <string name="network_required_title">To %1$s, this needs to go online</string>
    <string name="network_required_body">This keyboard is fully offline out of the box, so it has not asked any server for anything yet. To %1$s it has to fetch files from the internet. Turn on the switch below and it starts; turn it off when you are done and you are back to fully offline.</string>
    <string name="network_required_cost">The honest cost: once a connection happens, your network — your carrier, whoever owns the Wi-Fi, anyone in between — learns that this device reached a domain like github.com. The requests we send do not carry this app\'s name, but DNS lookups and TLS connection targets are in the clear by design. We cannot hide that, and we are not going to pretend otherwise. If you are somewhere that even “which keyboard is installed” is awkward to reveal, leave this switch alone — everything that works offline is already complete.</string>
    <string name="network_required_action">Turn on network</string>

    <string name="network_what_download_keyboards">download keyboards</string>
    <string name="network_what_browse">browse keyboards</string>
    <string name="network_what_check_updates">check for updates</string>

    <!-- ⚠ 誠實說明卡。這一段是產品定位的核心，要讀起來像一個坦率的工程師寫的。 -->
    <string name="first_run_title">This keyboard does not go online by default</string>
    <string name="first_run_body_1">We do not connect on our own. Typing, picking characters, changing input method, changing layout — all of it happens on your device.</string>
    <string name="first_run_body_2">If you want more input methods, or want to hear about updates, you can turn the switch on whenever you like; turn it off and you are back to fully offline. It ships off.</string>
    <string name="first_run_body_3">One thing we should say plainly: on Android, network permission is granted at install time and cannot be taken back while the app is running. So you will see it in your phone\'s permission list whether the switch is on or off. Since “no permission” is not something we can honestly offer, we made it checkable instead — the whole app has exactly one way out to the network, and while the switch is off that one way refuses outright. Every connection that really happens goes into the log on the Network page: when, to whom, what for, and how it went.</string>
    <string name="first_run_confirm">Got it — stay offline</string>

    <string name="honesty_title">Why “network access” is still in the permission list</string>
    <string name="honesty_body">Because on Android that permission is granted at install time and cannot be taken back while the app is running. As long as this app carries a keyboard store and in-app updates, it will be in the list — switch off or not. We are not going to claim we have no network permission; that claim falls apart the moment anybody checks.</string>
    <string name="honesty_checkable_title">So we made it checkable instead</string>
    <!-- 檔案路徑刻意留原文：它是要拿去 grep 的，翻譯了就找不到。 -->
    <string name="honesty_checkable_body">· The whole app has exactly one way out to the network: android/app/src/main/java/org/luminakey/ime/net/NetworkGate.kt in the source.\n· While the switch is off, that one way out refuses and throws. Not a single connection is opened.\n· Every connection that really got made is listed below, and each hop of a redirect gets its own line.\n· The log holds nothing you typed, and no URL paths — only host names and the reason.</string>
    <!-- %1$s = 紀錄檔的絕對路徑。 -->
    <string name="honesty_log_file">Log file: %1$s</string>

